{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## The defect\n\nThe MCP server resolves commits against its own code clone at `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code`. That\nclone is not fetched before a completion precheck, so it can lag `origin/main`. When it does, a close\nrouted through MCP for work whose commit HAS merged is refused with \"no commit references it\" — the\nprecheck cannot see a commit that demonstrably exists.\n\nObserved 2026-09-05 while closing `5310-b51f-bba6-4e61`: the MCP path could not resolve the merged\nSHAs and refused the close. The agent did NOT force it. It fell back to the local `rebar` CLI from a\nworktree that provably contained the commits, and the same close passed — which is sound, because the\nprecheck is explicitly a worktree-HEAD reachability check and the local worktree satisfied it\nhonestly.\n\n## Why this matters more than a one-off annoyance\n\nAGENTS.md directs agents to route tracker operations THROUGH the MCP server, with the local CLI as\nthe carve-out for local-code ops. So the documented primary path is the one that fails, and it fails\nprecisely on the most common case: closing a ticket shortly after its change merges. The refusal\nmessage names the ticket's evidence (\"no commit references it\") rather than the server's own staleness,\nso it reads as a defect in the work rather than in the resolver — which invites exactly the wrong\nresponse.\n\nThe correct fallback exists and worked here, but it depends on the agent knowing that the local CLI\nis legitimate for this and that the refusal was not about their commit. An agent that believed the\nrefusal would either re-push, re-verify, or reach for a bypass.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] The MCP server's commit resolution cannot silently use a stale clone: either it fetches before\n      resolving, or it detects staleness and says so. State which and why.\n- [x] A refusal caused by the server being unable to SEE a commit is distinguishable in its message\n      from a refusal caused by no commit referencing the ticket. The two are different conditions and\n      currently render identically.\n- [x] Defect-seeded: with the clone deliberately behind a merged commit, confirm the new behaviour\n      (fetch-then-resolve, or an explicit staleness error) rather than the misleading refusal. An\n      unobserved fix is not evidence.\n- [x] The legitimate local-CLI fallback is documented where an agent hitting this will find it, so the\n      recovery does not depend on someone having seen it before.\n- [x] Portability: no dependence on any single CI provider trigger.\n\n## Testing\n\n1. RED first: put the clone behind a merged commit and reproduce the current misleading refusal.\n2. Confirm a genuinely unreferenced ticket still refuses, with its own distinct message — the fix must\n   not make the real condition unreportable.\n3. Confirm a current clone still closes normally.\n\n## Provenance\n\nFound by an agent closing three merged tickets on 2026-09-05. It reported the refusal, declined to\nforce, and used the sanctioned fallback — so no damage resulted, but only because it reasoned\ncorrectly about a message that pointed the wrong way.\n\n## Completion evidence\n\n- Implemented fetch-before-resolve for stale code clones in `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`, reusing the existing remote probe/refresh helpers and rescanning upstream refs only after local evidence is absent.\n- Added distinct freshness/staleness messaging for an unrefreshable or unknown remote state while preserving the ordinary proven-absence refusal when refresh succeeds and no commit references the ticket.\n- Added defect-seeded and regression tests in `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py` for stale clone refresh, refreshed absence, and unrefreshable clone.\n- Documented the deterministic close precheck and local CLI fallback in `docs/plan-review-gate.md`.\n- Verified locally with targeted tests, `make check`, and full `make verify`; Gerrit change 2733 merged after LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788763334683740001,"uuid":"89cdf1d6-b72b-4bf3-939f-230ae16101e1"}